  "notes": "Dance-adjacent R&B-pop with a dancer's rhythmic phrasing, straight 2&4 with \"heavy 16th displacement\". The drum block is the entry's clearest claim and is authored as written: \"clipped, dry kick and clap with a syncopated 16th-note percussion bed; the pattern leaves deliberate holes on downbeats so the vocal lands in the gaps. No trap roll vocabulary — the density comes from percussion, not hats.\" So `kick.beatSkipProb` is 0.3 with a high syncopation, `percs.densityPerBar` runs 4—7 at `offbeat` placement (the highest perc density in this section) while `hihat.fillDensity` drops to 0.2 and `rolls.freqPerBar` is 0, and the snare carries a hard transient with a short tail. The low end is a synth sub, not an 808, so no `bass808` block exists: \"sub-heavy synth bass in short staccato 16ths, phrased as a rhythmic partner to the vocal rather than a sustained pad\" is `independent_riff` at a low `followRootsProb` with staccato cell shapes, and \"low end drops out entirely for pre-choruses\" is the deep arrangement drop-out. Key and range are documented — the flagship is F♯ minor and the working span F♯3—D5 is \"written mostly in the lower half\" — so the melody register ceiling is a hard 74 and `octaveJumpProb` stays low except for the noted falsetto flips. \"Short, breathy, rhythmically syncopated cells with whispered doubles and a spoken aside\" is the small `motifPitchCount` plus `endVariation`. `bpm.mode` 111 is the entry's own stated flagship tempo. The documented \"percussion-only breakdown before the last chorus\" is the `bridge` slot in the higher-weighted structure: engine/src/arrange.rs has no breakdown section kind and nothing strips a section to percussion, so a short bridge before the final chorus is the closest available encoding rather than a literal one. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize block and the perc gain; the research explicitly says the drum specifics are \"partially inferred\", which is also why `confidence` is medium against its high-medium rating. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED beyond its first value: the entry names only \"the flagship is F♯ minor\", so B minor, C minor and A minor are neighbouring minor tonics chosen so the key does not pin to a single value, and none of the three appears in the research.",
